    <h1>Pregnancy Week by Week</h1>

    <p>Pregnancy lasts about 40 weeks, counted from the first day of your last menstrual period (LMP). Here is what happens at each stage, for both you and your baby.</p>

    <h2>First Trimester (Weeks 1-13)</h2>

    <h3>Weeks 1-4</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> You may not know you are pregnant. Some women experience implantation bleeding.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Fertilization occurs around week 2. The blastocyst implants in the uterine lining by week 4.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 5-8</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Missed period, breast tenderness, nausea, fatigue, frequent urination.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Neural tube forms, heart begins to beat, arm and leg buds appear. Embryo is about the size of a kidney bean by week 8.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 9-13</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Nausea may peak, fatigue continues, breasts may be tender.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> All major organs have formed. Fingers and toes are visible. Embryo becomes a fetus at week 11 (ACOG).</p>

    <AdUnit slot="925728676" format="auto" />
    <h2>Second Trimester (Weeks 14-27)</h2>

    <h3>Weeks 14-16</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Energy returns, nausea fades, you may start to show.</p>

    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is about 3.5 inches long. Baby can make facial expressions.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 17-20</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Quickening (first movement) typically 16-22 weeks. You may feel fluttering or bubbling.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is about 6.5 inches long. Baby can hear sounds. Anatomy scan at 18-22 weeks.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 21-24</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Back pain, round ligament pain, heartburn, nasal congestion.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is about 12 inches long. Baby's lungs are developing. Baby has sleep-wake cycles.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 25-27</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Leg cramps, Braxton Hicks contractions, shortness of breath.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is about 14 inches long. Baby's eyes can open. Baby can respond to light.</p>

    <h2>Third Trimester (Weeks 28-40)</h2>

    <h3>Weeks 28-32</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Shortness of breath, frequent urination, heartburn, swelling, Braxton Hicks contractions.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is about 15 inches long. Baby weighs about 2.5 pounds. Baby can open and close eyes.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 33-36</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Lightening (baby dropping), increased pelvic pressure, difficulty sleeping.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is about 17-18.5 inches long. Baby weighs about 4-6 pounds. Baby's lungs are nearly mature.</p>

    <h3>Weeks 37-40</h3>
    <p><strong>Your body:</strong> Full term at 37 weeks. You may experience signs of labor: regular contractions, water breaking, bloody show.</p>
    <p><strong>Your baby:</strong> Baby is full term. Baby's organs are fully mature. Baby is about 18.5-20 inches long and weighs about 6-7.5 pounds.</p>

